% Number 87. Chace vol. II pl. 108 (photograph XXX), PDF pp. 263-264; Peet pp. 129-131 (Pl. Y).
% Not a computation: dated entries written on the verso, military and weather events.
% Red in Chace is in braces.
No. 87
{"Year 11, month 2 of Shomu,"} "was entered Onu."   % Onu = Heliopolis
{"Month 1 of Akhet, day 23,"} "attacked (?) the commander of the army against Zaru."   % Chace reads mr ms', Peet pn-rsy (?) on his Plate Y; Peet: "Reading very uncertain"
{"Day 25,"} "heard one to say, is entered Zaru."
{"Year 11, month 1 of Akhet, [day] 3, birth"} "of Seth; there was a causing [that hear] one voice his by the majesty of god this."   % Peet: a sign "must have been omitted"
{"Birth"} "of Isis; made heaven rain."
